          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.259,
            0.882,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Chapter 2 of Ganita Manjari, Part I, we explored linear patterns and learnt about linear polynomials. In this chapter, we will go a step further in exploring linear equations in two variables, by learning how to solve a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pair",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of linear equations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.362,
            0.615,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.1 Linear Equations in Two Variables"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.395,
            0.518,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Radha stops at a fruit cart. The price tags say that mangoes cost ₹60 per kg and bananas cost ₹50 per kg. She buys some kilograms of mangoes and some kilograms of bananas. Altogether, she pays ₹280. Can we express this situation as an equation?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.529,
            0.519,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since we do not know how many kilograms of mangoes or bananas she bought, let us assume that"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.532,
            0.396,
            0.907,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.532,
                0.396,
                0.907,
                0.622
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.592,
            0.518,
            0.632
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "x = number of kilograms of mangoes"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.636,
            0.546,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y = number of kilograms of bananas"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.661,
            0.881,
            0.72
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The cost of the mangoes is ₹60x and the cost of the bananas is ₹50y. The total cost is ₹280. Hence, we can express this using the linear equation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.719,
            0.585,
            0.738
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_0_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "60x + 50y = 280."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.743,
            0.881,
            0.8
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Notice that the left-hand side (LHS) and the right-hand side (RHS) of the equation both represent the same quantity, that is, the total cost (in ₹)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.801,
            0.88,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "60x + 50y = 280"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "linear equation in two variables",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
